To make CAL:9 deterministic, the validator could enforce invariants such as:

* Every registry object has a unique identifier.
* Every identifier resolves to a schema.
* Every schema validates successfully.
* Every binary has a recorded version and cryptographic hash.
* Every SDK references an official provenance source.
* Every dependency appears in the SBOM.
* Every artifact is either signed or explicitly exempted.
* Every exception includes a justification and expiration.
* Every audit report is reproducible from the recorded evidence.
* No executable artifact is promoted unless validation succeeds.

